---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import StructuredData from '../components/StructuredData.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Premium Domain Valuation Guide 2026 | aic.contact';
const description =
  'How premium domain names are valued: length, TLD, meaning, comps, and investment outlook. Why aic.contact is priced at $4,444 with escrow-protected transfer.';
const ogImage = 'https://imagedelivery.net/-sPAUAWeA405NiWJ0SNIQA/581e6a5a-e4eb-4a01-a5d3-e85e52022d00/public';
const canonical = `${SITE_URL}/valuation-guide/`;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What makes a domain name premium?',
    a: 'Short length, a trusted or meaningful TLD, built-in semantic meaning, easy spelling and recall, clean history, and comparable sales support. aic.contact scores on all five: 3 letters, a .contact TLD that literally means contact, and instant AI relevance.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How are investment domains priced?',
    a: 'Sellers weigh character count, TLD liquidity, keyword demand, brandability, past comparable sales, and holding costs. Ultra-short names in growing verticals like AI typically carry scarcity premiums because supply is fixed at one per string.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are expired domains a good alternative?',
    a: 'Expired domains can carry backlink equity but often bring spam history, trademark risk, and cleanup costs. A clean-title premium like aic.contact avoids those risks with immediate, transferable ownership.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is aic.contact listed at $4,444?',
    a: 'Three-letter domains rarely trade at four figures, and AI-relevant names command more. $4,444 reflects comparable short-brandable sales, the built-in "AI Contact" meaning, and instant-use utility for consulting, agencies, and personal brands — with escrow protection included.',
  },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage}>
  <SEO slot="head" title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} pathname="/valuation-guide/" keywords="premium domain names, domain valuation guide, investment domains, expired domains, buy .contact domains, brandable domains" />
  <StructuredData
    slot="head"
    schema={{
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@graph': [
        {
          '@type': 'Article',
          '@id': `${canonical}#article`,
          headline: 'Premium Domain Valuation Guide',
          description: description,
          image: ogImage,
          author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'aic.contact', url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
          publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'aic.contact', url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
          mainEntityOfPage: canonical,
          datePublished: '2026-06-01',
          dateModified: '2026-10-01',
        },
        {
          '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
          '@id': `${canonical}#breadcrumb`,
          itemListElement: [
            { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE_URL}/` },
            { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Valuation Guide', item: canonical },
          ],
        },
        {
          '@type': 'FAQPage',
          '@id': `${canonical}#faq`,
          mainEntity: faqs.map((item) => ({
            '@type': 'Question',
            name: item.q,
            acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
          })),
        },
      ],
    }}
  />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-32 pb-16">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm text-white/50 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-white min-h-[48px] inline-flex items-center">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="mx-2">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page" class="text-white/80">Valuation Guide</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="inline-block px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-white/5 text-xs tracking-[1.5px] font-medium text-white/60 mb-4">DOMAIN INVESTING · 6 MIN READ</div>
    <h1 class="section-header tracking-[-0.04em] mb-4">Premium domain valuation guide.</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-white/70 mb-10">How serious buyers underwrite names like <strong class="text-white">aic.contact</strong> — and why scarcity plus meaning drives price.</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-3">1. Length and memorability</h2>
        <p>Every character removed increases recall and type-in value. Three-letter domains are a fixed-supply asset class — only 17,576 combinations per TLD exist, and most are held long-term. Short, pronounceable strings like AIC clear the bar that long multi-word brandables never reach.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-3">2. TLD fit and meaning</h2>
        <p>.contact is a semantic TLD: it tells visitors what to do. Paired with AIC (Artificial Intelligence Contact), the full string reads as a complete value proposition rather than an abbreviation needing explanation. Names where the TLD completes the meaning consistently outperform random-pair names.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-3">3. Comparable sales</h2>
        <p>Underwrite against public short-domain and AI-vertical sales, not asking prices. Our <a href="/comparable-sales/" data-cta="guide-comps" class="text-[#22f5ff] hover:underline font-medium">comparable sales breakdown</a> shows how 3-letter and AI-relevant names trade, and where $4,444 sits in that range.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-3">4. Investment vs. expired domains</h2>
        <p>Expired domains can look cheap until diligence: toxic backlinks, prior trademarks, and de-indexation risk. Investment-grade premiums are priced for clean title, immediate transfer, and zero remediation — the difference between an asset and a project.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-3">5. Utility from day one</h2>
        <p>aic.contact works as a consultancy home, an agency brand, a personal platform (you@aic.contact), or a product contact layer. Domains with immediate multi-use utility hold value better than single-use novelties.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal glass rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-10 mt-12 text-center">
      <div class="text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tighter">$4,444 <span class="text-lg text-white/50 font-normal">USD</span></div>
      <p class="text-white/60 mt-2 mb-6">One-time · Full ownership · Escrow.com protected</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="mailto:sales@desertrich.com?subject=Buy%20Now%20—%20aic.contact%20($4,444)&body=Hello,%0D%0A%0D%0AI%20want%20to%20buy%20aic.contact%20now%20at%20$4,444.%20Please%20open%20escrow.%0D%0A%0D%0ABest%20regards," data-cta="guide-buy-now" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 min-h-[48px] py-3.5 rounded-2xl bg-white text-[#0a0a0f] font-semibold hover:bg-white/90 transition-all">Buy Now — $4,444</a>
        <a href="/#inquire" data-cta="guide-make-offer" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 min-h-[48px] py-3.5 rounded-2xl border border-white/20 hover:bg-white/5 font-medium transition-all">Make an Offer</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm"><a href="/" data-cta="guide-home" class="text-[#22f5ff] hover:underline">← Back to aic.contact</a></p>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="guide-faq">
      <h2 id="guide-faq" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-5">Valuation FAQ</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="group glass rounded-2xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer px-6 py-5 select-none min-h-[48px]">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg tracking-tight text-white/90 group-open:text-white">{item.q}</h3>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-white/50 text-2xl leading-none group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="px-6 pb-5 -mt-1 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
